docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:1:# Fluorite & Shrine Lighting System
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:5:Three interlocking systems that make shrines feel alive and give fluorite a unique mechanical identity rooted in its real-world physics (fluorescence — the word literally comes from this mineral).
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:9:## Shrine Lighting (T1–T5)
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:11:### T1 — Deity Standing → Shrine Color & Radius
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:13:Shrine light is no longer static. It reads the player's normalized deity standing (−1 to +1) and adjusts each frame.
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:23:Standing state is stored in `_shrineLightStates` (keyed by shrine entity ID), updated from `shrine:combat:scaling` events. Clears on floor transition.
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:27:On `shrine:communion`:
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:28:- **Blessing** → 0.8s gold bloom, radius 6 at shrine position
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:31:Also records `_lastShrineTouched` (per player) for miracle beam targeting.
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:33:### T3 — Shrine Charges Fluorite Gems
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:35:Holy light is treated as UV-adjacent (divine energy ≈ energetic radiation). Fluorite gems placed near a shrine slowly charge to full cyan glow.
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:44:On `shrine:combat:scaling`:
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:45:- **Divine favor** (`mult > 1`) → 0.28s gold burst at shrine, radius 3.5
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:46:- **Divine wrath** (`mult < 1`) → 0.28s red flash at shrine, radius 3.5
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:47:- Also updates `_shrineLightStates` with the numeric standing value
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:51:On `deity:intervention` with `kind: 'shrine_blessing'`:
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:52:- Holy beam drawn from shrine → player (uses existing `_holyBeams` system)
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:53:- Radiant bloom (radius 7, `HOLY_GOLD`) at shrine position
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:62:Fluorite absorbs divine and electric energy, stores it as charge stacks, then releases as a blinding cyan flash on the next strike. The charging sources mirror real fluorescence physics: energetic radiation (lightning) charges it fast; ambient divine light (shrine) charges it slowly.
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:75:| Fighting near shrine in divine favor | +1 | Per combat hit while `shrine:combat:scaling` fires with `mult > 1` |
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:76:| Shrine ambient glow (floor gem) | Slow | T3 above — for gems on the floor, not socketed |
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:103:Absorbs electric energy (taking lightning damage, fighting near a shrine in good standing).
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:111:When the player kills an enemy near a shrine while in high standing, there is a 12% chance the deity manifests a fluorite stone at the player's feet.
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:115:- Nearest shrine within 5 tiles (Chebyshev)
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:130:Shrine glows brighter when favored
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:132:Shrine holy light charges nearby fluorite gems (visual glow)
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:134:Fighting near shrine in divine favor charges socketed fluorite (+1/hit)
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:136:Taking lightning damage near shrine charges it faster (+2/hit)
docs/systems/FLUORITE_SHRINE_SYSTEM.md:140:Killing near shrine with high standing → 12% chance deity gifts another fluorite
